# Messages for orders.v1. See README.md for the file format.
#
# Every line is: headers \t key \t value. The literal two characters \t are the field separator,
# not a real tab, so that this file survives being opened in any editor. seed.sh turns them into
# real tabs before handing the line to Kafka's console producer.
#
# %TS-n% is replaced with an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp n seconds before the seed runs, so the data
# looks like it was produced by a system that is running now rather than one frozen in 2026.
#
# The payloads deliberately do not all have the same fields: `orders` in a real system grows new
# ones over time and old messages never gain them. A message browser has to cope with that.
#mode: headers-key-value

